       21  St Andrews Lutheran Church in Malahang , Morobe Province . Christianity is the main religion in Papua New Guinea
       22  Religion in Papua New Guinea is dominated by various branches of Christianity , with traditional animism and ancestor worship often occurring less openly as another layer underneath or more openly side by side with Christianity. The Catholic Church has a plurality of the population. The courts, gove
       23  A large majority of Papua New Guineans identify themselves as members of a Christian church (96% in the decennial 2000 census); however, many combine their Christian faith with traditional indigenous practices, known as religious syncretism . [ 4 ]
       24  Other religions represented in the country include the Baháʼí Faith , Hinduism and Islam . [ 4 ]
